WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.429
JAMIE: The compliance officer I pictured
earlier? She's now on her third coffee

00:00:03.429 --> 00:00:06.858
JAMIE: and she's drawn a very large
diagram.

00:00:06.923 --> 00:00:09.667
RUFUS: With several question marks where
the arrows should be.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:13.546
JAMIE: Though a domestic model's servers
being in Palo Alto isn't the same

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:17.212
JAMIE: legal and jurisdictional risk as
servers subject to Chinese law.

00:00:17.277 --> 00:00:18.436
RUFUS: No, that's a fair distinction.

00:00:18.616 --> 00:00:22.435
ALEX: And AP is clear this is a federal
civilian-agency action. Not a

00:00:22.435 --> 00:00:26.255
ALEX: consumer ban. But if you sell
software to the federal government, you

00:00:26.255 --> 00:00:30.074
ALEX: need to audit whether DeepSeek is
anywhere in your stack — because

00:00:30.074 --> 00:00:33.894
ALEX: if it is, you have a procurement
problem.
